admin -> sys.ticketing.close
admin -> sys.ticketing.ongoing
admin -> sys.admin_uc.manage_emp
admin -> sys.admin_uc.manage_users
admin -> sys.admin_uc.manage_lookup
admin -> sys.admin_uc.config_sync
admin -> sys.reporting.dashboard
admin -> sys.reporting.report
admin -> sys.reporting.backfill

sys.reporting.sync -> sheets: "writes rows"
sys.reporting.backfill -> sheets: "writes history"
sys.auth -> idp: "verifies credentials"

# --- include / extend ---
sys.ticketing.encode -> sys.ticketing.gennum: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.encode -> sys.ticketing.resolve_emp: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.encode -> sys.ticketing.audit: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.encode -> sys.ticketing.enqueue: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.update -> sys.ticketing.audit: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.update -> sys.ticketing.enqueue: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.assign -> sys.ticketing.audit: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.close -> sys.ticketing.audit: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.ongoing -> sys.ticketing.audit: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.enqueue -> sys.reporting.sync: "«trigger»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.ticketing.resolve_emp -> sys.admin_uc.manage_emp: "«extend»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}

sys.ticketing.encode -> sys.auth: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}
sys.admin_uc.manage_users -> sys.auth: "«include»" {style.stroke-dash: 3}

legend: |||md
  **Legend**

  | | Meaning |
  |---|---|
  | Dark blue oval | Confirmed use case |
  | Light blue oval | Included use case — never invoked directly by an actor |
  | **Amber oval** | **Awaiting a decision from the 11FTC IT team** |
  | Dashed association | Proposed, not yet confirmed |

  **Notes**

  - **Employee is not a system actor.** They report a concern to a person; IT Staff
    encodes it. No employee login exists. The dashed association to IT Staff is a
    real-world interaction outside the system boundary.
  - **Synchronize to Sheet has no human actor.** It is triggered by the system when a
    ticket is written, never invoked by a user.
  - **There is no *Void Ticket* and no *Resolve Ticket*.** The department has three
    statuses — Open, Ongoing, Closed. Closing *is* resolving, and mis-encoded tickets
    are corrected by *Update Ticket*, not voided.
  - **Amber items:** *View Dashboard* is shown for IT Staff as a proposal;
    *Manage Lookups* has no content until the IT team supplies the department and
    issue-category lists.

  Requirement IDs, SRS sections, and open-item references for every use case above
  are in **`12-traceability-matrix.md`**.
||| {near: bottom-center; shape: text}
